{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>The Rock, His deed is perfect.</b> This refers to what is above — to the heavens and the earth and the four directions." "<b>His deed is perfect.</b> His deeds are with perfection and completeness — not like the measure of HaShem [compared to] the measure of flesh and blood. The measure of flesh and blood: when a man builds a building, his deed is not perfect and complete, for he did not make the wood and the stones and the dust, but only arranged them one upon another. But HaShem — His deed is perfect and complete, for He creates everything." "<b>For all His ways are justice.</b> Because He intends to tell how He took vengeance on Israel first, and afterward on other nations — He first justifies the judgment concerning Israel, for all His affairs are with justice and righteousness, as He goes on to explain."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:59.678397835Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}